{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"As of **6 November 2026**, distinguish two levels under the Central Bank of Ireland’s UCITS Q&A:\n\n- **Mixed umbrella:** Where only some sub-funds are ETFs, use **“UCITS ETF” at the relevant ETF sub-fund level**, not as an umbrella-wide designation implying that every sub-fund is an ETF. Non-ETF sibling sub-funds must not be labelled ETFs.\n- **Sub-fund with listed and unlisted classes:** Irish guidance permits **“UCITS ETF” at the listed share-class level**, rather than requiring it in the sub-fund’s name. Identify the listed classes accordingly in the relevant documentation; do not extend that designation to unlisted classes.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Sub-fund identification distinguishes ETF from non-ETF compartments; listed-class identification distinguishes exchange-traded from unlisted access within the same portfolio. Sharing a portfolio does not make an unlisted class an ETF class."}}
